*Modules affected*: 11 TOKENS_ECONOMY, 13 PACKAGES, 16 REFERRAL_SYSTEM, 23 WEBHOOK_SERVER, 24B PAYMENT_CALLBACKS

*Bug 2.1: `add_tokens` acquires `_get_uid_lock` then starts SERIALIZABLE TX. Webhook acquires TX then `_get_uid_lock`*  
Where: 11 `add_tokens` acquires lock before `db.begin()`. 23 `alby_webhook` does `async with db.begin()` first, then `async with uid_lock`.  
What: Opposite lock order. Under burst: T1 holds uid_lock waiting for DB row lock. T2 holds DB row lock waiting for uid_lock.  
When: Webhook fires for user while user simultaneously clicks "Buy" -> `activate_package` or `add_tokens` from admin.  
Who: Any user during payment + package activation.  
Impact: Postgres 40001 serialization failure triggers retries. With 5 retries and jitter it usually resolves, but under 500+ concurrent it can exhaust all retries and return False. Payment marked paid but tokens not credited.  
Severity: *2. Persistent lock* - DB: `paid=true, tokens_credited=false`. Needs manual `recover_missing_webhook_jobs`.

*Bug 2.2: `activate_package` calls `is_user_locked_for_buy` which opens NEW db session*  
Where: 13 `activate_package` -> `is_user_locked_for_buy(uid, db)`  
What: `is_user_locked_for_buy` ignores passed `db` and opens its own `SessionLocal()`. So lock check is not in same TX as deduction.  
When: User buys package at exact moment buy lock expires.  
Who: User at end of 10min lock window.  
Impact: Race: lock check passes, then before deduction another invoice is created. You can end with negative token balance despite `ck_users_tokens_nonnegative` because deduction and lock check were not atomic.  
Severity: *2. Persistent lock* - DB constraint violation raises, TX rolls back, but user state may be `pending_pkg` and never cleared.

ROOT CAUSE GROUP 3: INVOICE REUSE / EXPIRY LOGIC MISMATCH
*Modules affected*: 24B PAYMENT_CALLBACKS, 17A ALBY_CLIENT, 26 USER_AND_PAYMENT_LIFECYCLE

*Bug 3.1: `cb_buy_confirm_yes` deletes expired invoice but doesn't clear `uq_one_unpaid_invoice`*  
Where: 24B `_verify_with_alby_and_delete_if_expired` -> `DELETE FROM payments`  
What: Partial unique index `uq_one_unpaid_invoice` is on `(uid) WHERE paid=false AND state IN ('reserving','open')`. Delete removes row, good. But if webhook arrives between SELECT FOR UPDATE and DELETE, webhook sets `paid=true` and now DELETE deletes a paid row.  
When: User clicks buy, invoice expired on Alby side, webhook for old invoice arrives late.  
Who: User with expired invoice who retries buy.  
Impact: You delete a `paid` payment. Tokens never credited because `add_tokens` never ran. `paid=true` row gone, no recovery path.  
Severity: *2. Persistent lock* - Money taken by Alby, no tokens. Only fixable by manual DB insert + credit.

*Bug 3.2: `reconcile_reserving_payments` marks `state='dead'` but `uq_one_unpaid_invoice` still blocks new invoice*  
Where: 17A + 26 `reconcile_reserving_payments`  
What: Index only covers `paid=false AND state IN (reserving,open)`. `dead` is outside index, so new invoice can be created. But 24B SELECT for reuse looks for `state IN ('reserving','open')`. So dead rows are ignored, good. Problem: `create_invoice` ON CONFLICT is on `client_ref` which is globally unique. If boot marked old `reserving` to `dead`, new `create_invoice` generates new uuid so fine. But if Alby later sends webhook for that `dead` client_ref, webhook fallback will try to UPDATE `state='reserving'` row that is now `dead` and will fail, returns 409.  
When: Bot restart during invoice creation.  
Who: User whose invoice was in flight during restart.  
Impact: Webhook dropped. Payment never transitions to `open`. User must create new invoice.  
Severity: *1. Permanent lock* - No DB corruption, just lost webhook.

ROOT CAUSE GROUP 4: `processed_job_id` CLAIM RACE + UNIQUE VIOLATION
*Modules affected*: 23 WEBHOOK_SERVER, 26 USER_AND_PAYMENT_LIFECYCLE

*Bug 4.1: `_enqueue_job` uses `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` but returns None, webhook treats as already processed*  
Where: 23 `_enqueue_job`  
What: If 2 webhooks race, second gets `job_id=None` and returns 200 immediately per FIX #MIT1-4. But first webhook may crash after enqueue but before `add_tokens`. Now job exists with `status=pending` but no one will process it because second webhook bailed.  
When: Duplicate webhook delivery from Alby.  
Who: Any paying user.  
Impact: Payment stays `open, paid=false`. `recover_missing_webhook_jobs` only picks `paid=true`. So it never recovers.  
Severity: *2. Persistent lock* - DB: stuck `open` payment. Requires manual flip to `paid=true` + credit.

